  "date_published": "2013-10-09",
  "description": "The Málaga Stereo and Laser Urban Data Set was gathered entirely in urban scenarios in Málaga (Spain) with a car equipped with a Bumblebee 2 stereo camera, five laser scanners (three Hokuyo UTM-30LX and two SICK LMS-200), an Xsens MTi inertial measurement unit and a GPS receiver. It contains high-resolution (1024x768) color stereo images grabbed at 20 fps during a 36.8 km, about 1.5 hour trajectory with real-life traffic, which makes it a suitable benchmark for SLAM, visual odometry, loop closure, place recognition and object detection. Data is provided as plain text files and as binary MRPT rawlog files, both for the entire dataset and for 15 selected extracts, together with raw and rectified images and calibration files.",
