  "date_published": "2009-11",
  "description": "The Málaga 2009 Robotic Dataset Collection contains six outdoor datasets (PARKING-0L, PARKING-2L, PARKING-6L, CAMPUS-0L, CAMPUS-2L and CAMPUS-RT) recorded in November 2008 at the University of Málaga (Spain) with an electric vehicle equipped with three SICK and two Hokuyo laser scanners, two color cameras, an Xsens IMU and three RTK GPS receivers. A centimeter-level 6D ground truth of the vehicle path, with its uncertainty, is computed from the RTK GPS data, which makes the collection suitable as a test bed for visual SLAM, 2D SLAM, visual odometry and localization. Reference 3D point clouds built from the lasers are also provided.",
