  "date_published": "2024-01-31",
  "description": "The GREENBOT dataset is a multimodal mobile robotics dataset recorded inside a typical Mediterranean greenhouse with tomato crops, a challenging environment where GNSS accuracy is degraded by the structure and the crop. A sensorised cart carrying a Velodyne VLP-16 LiDAR, an Ouster OS0 LiDAR with IMU, a Bumblebee BB2 stereo camera and a NovAtel GNSS/IMU was moved through all the corridors of the greenhouse in nine sequences. It is available as ROS 1 Noetic bags and MRPT rawlogs (for ROS 2 Humble), with calibration files and the tools to run MOLA SLAM. It is the first dataset suitable to test SLAM methods in a greenhouse environment.",
